  {
   "id": "adr-decision",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 40,
   "y": 1359.0,
   "width": 1500,
   "height": 334.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
   "backgroundColor": "#d3f9d8",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 1961388059,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1241425228,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "id": "adr-decision-text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "adr-decision-text",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 46,
   "y": 1365.0,
   "width": 1488,
   "height": 320.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1464878945,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 976960453,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "We choose B, central model + source adapters, because it is the only option that gives every check all documents linked to a trial (quality), lets reviewers and check\nread the same evidence (risk, ADR-001), and records who did what (traceability). Its cost is a one-off rebuild, which we take now while the local data is reset\nanyway.\n1. Sources: a source table (registry, publication index, manual, gold); every stored record carries (source, the source's own key), unique, so re-fetching versions it\ninstead of duplicating it.\n2. Trials: trial = our id; trial_identifier (scheme, normalised value) is unique and points to one trial; trial_record = what one source says, versioned. Ingest\nmatches all identifiers: none \u2192 new trial, one trial \u2192 attach, several \u2192 a possible duplicate for a person; merges are recorded and reversible.\n3. Documents in three layers: file (bytes, by sha256, stored once) \u2192 document (logical, identity = source key) \u2192 document version (replaced files kept, dated). Same\ntext in different bytes is flagged by a page-text fingerprint. Trial \u2194 document links carry role, basis (listed by the registry, identifier in the text, by hand),\nsource and confidence; a check reads the current version of every linked document and records which.\n4. Audit: actors (people and processes); an append-only audit log written by Postgres triggers in the same transaction; no update in place or hard delete without an\naudit entry.\n5. Gold datasets: dataset version (name, version, source, evidence scope) and items naming trials by identifier, with labels, comments and subsets (dev/test). An\nevaluation = dataset version + subset + pipeline configuration; it runs in its own database built from a bundle (trials, files, labels), so CI is reproducible and the\nworking database never holds benchmark data. CI replays stored model answers on every push and makes real model calls when prompts or model settings change, or by\nhand. Bruckner et al. is the first gold source.",
   "originalText": "We choose B, central model + source adapters, because it is the only option that gives every check all documents linked to a trial (quality), lets reviewers and check\nread the same evidence (risk, ADR-001), and records who did what (traceability). Its cost is a one-off rebuild, which we take now while the local data is reset\nanyway.\n1. Sources: a source table (registry, publication index, manual, gold); every stored record carries (source, the source's own key), unique, so re-fetching versions it\ninstead of duplicating it.\n2. Trials: trial = our id; trial_identifier (scheme, normalised value) is unique and points to one trial; trial_record = what one source says, versioned. Ingest\nmatches all identifiers: none \u2192 new trial, one trial \u2192 attach, several \u2192 a possible duplicate for a person; merges are recorded and reversible.\n3. Documents in three layers: file (bytes, by sha256, stored once) \u2192 document (logical, identity = source key) \u2192 document version (replaced files kept, dated). Same\ntext in different bytes is flagged by a page-text fingerprint. Trial \u2194 document links carry role, basis (listed by the registry, identifier in the text, by hand),\nsource and confidence; a check reads the current version of every linked document and records which.\n4. Audit: actors (people and processes); an append-only audit log written by Postgres triggers in the same transaction; no update in place or hard delete without an\naudit entry.\n5. Gold datasets: dataset version (name, version, source, evidence scope) and items naming trials by identifier, with labels, comments and subsets (dev/test). An\nevaluation = dataset version + subset + pipeline configuration; it runs in its own database built from a bundle (trials, files, labels), so CI is reproducible and the\nworking database never holds benchmark data. CI replays stored model answers on every push and makes real model calls when prompts or model settings change, or by\nhand. Bruckner et al. is the first gold source.",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": "adr-decision",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "h-consequences",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 40,
   "y": 1719.0,
   "width": 151.84,
   "height": 27.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 292348202,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1232703621,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Consequences",
   "originalText": "Consequences",
   "fontSize": 22,
   "fontFamily": 6,
